  "text": "A short written message; in music, a single sound.\n\nAn account of people and events, real or imagined.\n\nHold and move something from one place to another.\n\nThe surface of the footbridge that people walk on.\n\nPip takes Rina’s intact spare tile from the shelf.\n\nAnother page or version containing the same words.\n\nAfter waiting or after other things have happened.\n\nPip hands the spare tile to Sol beside his ladder.\n\nA container with a handle and a spout for pouring.\n\nBrought something to its intended person or place.\n\nPut a new or different thing in place of another.\n\nGrandma has Mara's page. Tell her what Mara said.\n\nHands something to someone or makes it available.\n\nPut something over an area to protect or hide it.\n\nA method of doing something or a path to a place.\n\nMicrophone off. You can listen to your recording.\n\nGrandma says: “I'd like to hear what Sol brings.”\n\nWhile something happens, or in the way described.\n\nA group of sentences about one part of a subject.\n\nPulled or took in; drew breath means breathed in.\n\nA structure that connects two sides across a gap.\n\nBelonging to the female person already mentioned.\n\nSpace or an opportunity for someone or something.\n\nPip will read Mara’s page. Mara is still at work.\n\nWords that tell a story or describe what happens.\n\nBoth sections are secure. Walk across to Grandma.\n\nSol says: “Thanks for letting me know. I’ll bring\n\nHad information or understanding about something.\n\nGrandma brings cushions back to the garden bench.\n\nTimes when someone goes to see a person or place.\n\nM56 174v-49m251 49v-49M56 135l15 23m236-23-15 23\n\nTell someone you are grateful for what they did.\n\nChoose a time and someone to share Mara’s story.\n\nEveryone knows the plan. Your friends are ready.\n\nTell Grandma what you learned and choose a plan.",
